Robert,

We agree with you about the word "audit." To an investor it can suggest that =
something has gone wrong, and that is not the impression we want the note to =
leave. We will describe the conversations instead as part of a periodic revie=
w of how Gallegos, Pope and Marsh communicates with the people who follow it,=
 which is accurate and, in our experience, far less likely to prompt an anxio=
us call.

We would also suggest one addition, if you are comfortable with it. A sentenc=
e stating that we will not discuss results, outlook, or anything the company =
has not already made public tends to put investors at ease, and it gives you =
some protection as well.

Michelle will send you the draft with both changes marked, so that you can ap=
prove it in a single pass.

Thanks


